# Pull a Claude Design file

Cursor does not have the design server, and it must not start a Claude chat to fetch one. `tools/pull_design.py` reads the server with the design login Claude Code already stored. Do not tell Anthony to save the HTML, and do not add the design MCP to Cursor.

When the update-window design is missing, or the user names a file in the Nebula design project:

```powershell
python tools/pull_design.py
python tools/pull_design.py --file "Nebula Toast Row.dc.html" --into design/toast-row
```

The first command needs no URL. It reads the design server directly with the Claude Code design login. It does not start a Claude chat. If it says the login is missing, stop. Do not build from a partial file.
